From 83832b9ce68b4fec6275539e88d82aea7acdd76e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rl-infra <rl-infra@localhost>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 14:04:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Tutoring environment: native multi-turn learner simulation in
 the Apertus 2 format

A native multi-turn environment (env name tutoring) adapted from NVIDIA NeMo UserSim
(Apache-2.0, general_educational probe) for the Apertus 2 message format. Each episode
reads the policy's reply frame (thinking dropped), calls the configured judge/learner
pool concurrently (async Ray actor with max_concurrency=1000) using append-only quoted
dialogue history and trailing role anchor/frustration, runs deterministic and LLM
learner-gate checks with retries, checks early stop from min_turns, enforces a
min_remaining_tokens margin so near-full dialogues trigger the final judge instead of
overflowing rollouts.py with reward 0, and scores completed dialogues on UserSim's axes
(multi-sample structured JSON average or deterministic first-token logprobs). Exhausted
gates, pool errors, and unparseable judge calls set mask_sample=True.

Adds processor apertus2_tutoring_data_processor (with optional per-row SystemPrompt
behavior injection) and unit tests with a fake OpenAI server.
